    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Rochester-NY/Admissions-Visit-Assistant_JR102766": {
      "title": "Admissions Visit Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights: Join a dynamic enrollment team dedicated to helping achieve RIT’s enrollment goals. In this role, you will support the enrollment team and in particular the events and visit team by greeting and checking-in our visitors. In addition, to serving as the front-desk specialist for our Bausch & Lomb Center they will coordinated tasks essential to delivering a high‑quality campus visit experience. This position offers the opportunity to make a direct impact on the institution’s student recruitment efforts through positive customer service and support of our visitors. Key responsibilities include: Visitor Experience & Front Desk Operations  — Serve as the primary front desk greeter, delivering a welcoming, organized, and service‑oriented lobby experience for all prospective students and families. Communication Management  — Manage and respond to visit‑related phone calls and emails to ensure timely, accurate support for visitors and campus partners. Visit Scheduling & Coordination  — Schedule daily campus visits and coordinate additional meetings with academic departments and other campus partners as needed. CRM & Data Management  — Utilize the department’s CRM to load visit events, process registrations, and run/resolve visit‑related queries to maintain accurate and efficient visit operations. Student Staff Oversight  — Train, supervise, and support front desk student workers to ensure consistent, high‑quality service and smooth daily operations. Materials & Hospitality Management  — Manage inventory and assembly of visit materials and oversee hospitality supplies to maintain a professional and welcoming environment.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Processes applications and related documents for various student types, ensuring accuracy and completeness Provides comprehensive guidance and support to prospective students and their families through multiple communication channels, including phone, email, and in-person interactions Manages the logistics of campus visits, ensuring a welcoming and informative experience for visitors Assists the admissions team with the preparation and execution of events, such as open houses, information sessions, and orientation programs Identifies and troubleshoots errors in the application process, implementing effective solutions to ensure smooth operations Maintains accurate and up-to-date records of applicant information and communication logs in the admissions database Works closely with other departments, such as financial aid, academic advising, and student services, to provide a seamless admissions experience Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of administrative processes, including supply ordering, inventory tracking, and facilities management Knowledge of admissions processes, including understanding the procedures and requirements for processing applications Knowledge of student information systems Skill in identifying issues in the application process and implementing solutions to ensure smooth operations Skill in providing support and creating positive experiences for prospective students and their families Ability to provide guidance and offer clear and accurate information to prospective students and their families about the admissions process Ability to quickly adjust to changes in procedures, policies, and technology used in the admissions process Minimum Education & Experience High School diploma or GED 1 year of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Operations, Administrative, Service, or Technical Support Level 1 - An entry-level role building knowledge and skills. Performs routine, well-defined, easy-to-understand tasks that can typically be learned in a short period of time. Work is performed under close supervision using clearly prescribed methods and detailed instructions. FLSA Category Non-Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $16.90 - $25.40 Hourly Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Rochester-NY/Program-Support-Coordinator-III_JR102800": {
      "title": "Program Support Coordinator III",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights Join the Alumni & Constituent Engagement team and play a key role in supporting programs, events, and communications that strengthen connections between RIT and its alumni, donors, volunteers, and friends. This position provides administrative, operational, and customer service support that helps ensure the successful execution of engagement initiatives and the day-to-day operations of the department. Key Responsibilities: Provide administrative and operational support for alumni, donor, and constituent events, including registration management, event materials preparation, logistics coordination, and event follow-up. Support engagement and outreach initiatives by preparing correspondence, maintaining event and volunteer records, and assisting with relationship-building efforts. Manage calendars, schedule meetings, coordinate appointments, reserve spaces, and support leadership scheduling needs. Assist with donor and constituent communications, including acknowledgements, invitations, event confirmations, and stewardship correspondence. Maintain accurate constituent records and documentation within university systems, ensuring data integrity and timely updates. Deliver exceptional customer service to alumni, donors, volunteers, and campus partners while handling sensitive information with professionalism and discretion. Collaborate with colleagues across University Advancement and campus partners to support engagement activities, events, and special projects. University Advancement | Alumni & Constituent Engagement University Advancement fosters meaningful connections between RIT and its alumni, donors, parents, friends, and community partners. Within University Advancement, the Alumni & Constituent Engagement team develops programs, events, communications, and volunteer opportunities that strengthen lifelong relationships with the university and inspire engagement with the RIT community. Through collaboration, service, and relationship-building, the team supports RIT's mission and helps create lasting impact for students, alumni, and the university.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Ensures the smooth operation of day-to-day office tasks by coordinating with other departments and assisting with various administrative functions as needed Handles front desk activities by greeting visitors, answering phones, and providing customer support. Serves as the 1st point of contact for assigned area Coordinates and manages calendars, scheduling appointments, interviews, travel, and events. Assisting with or coordinating the preparation/ turnover of meeting space or work/ desk space Prepares and distributes communications, including emails, memos, and reports, to various internal and external stakeholders Handles documents, files, and records, ensuring proper filing systems. Secures sensitive and confidential records. Collects data, maintains database records, and assists with data analysis as needed Manages office supplies, track inventory, and coordinate purchasing to maintain adequate resources for office operations Assists with HR-related functions, including employee hiring, onboarding, and payroll processing, ensuring adherence to institutional policies Processes expense reports, recording and receipting payments, creating invoices, and monitoring budgets. Provides purchasing support and p-card processes. Supports budget tracking, assisting with financial record-keeping and ensuring compliance with departmental budget guidelines Coordinates and assist with event planning and logistical support for meetings, conferences, and other departmental activities Assists in the preparation and organization of documents, presentations, and reports, ensuring they are accurate and timely Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of administrative processes, including supply ordering, inventory tracking, and facilities management Knowledge of human resources practices, including onboarding, payroll processing, and employee records management Skill in scheduling, organizing, and coordinating meetings, appointments, and events for multiple stakeholders Skill in handling and processing invoices, purchase orders, and expense reports with attention to detail and accuracy Ability to communicate clearly and professionally with internal and external stakeholders, addressing inquiries and providing assistance Ability to handle confidential information with discretion, ensuring compliance with organizational and legal privacy standards Minimum Education & Experience Associate's degree in related field 5 years of related experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Operations, Administrative, Service, or Technical Support Level 3 - Senior level role with considerable knowledge and skills. Performs complex tasks and project work. Work is typically not routine and requires troubleshooting and analysis. Mentors or guides less experienced staff. FLSA Category Non-Exempt Work Location Hybrid Compensation $19.65 - $31.45 USD Hourly Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
