    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Rochester-NY/Human-Resources-Business-Partner_JR102747": {
      "title": "Human Resources Business Partner",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis position is eligible to be hired at the HR Business Partner level II (Associate HR Business Partner) or III (HR Business Partner) based on experience and qualifications. Associate HR Business Partner Minimum Qualifications : Bachelor's degree in related field and 2 years of relevant experience. Salary Range: $65,000 - $85,000 HR Business Partner: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in related field and 5 years of relevant experience. Salary Range: $85,000 - $115,000   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Partners with business units, using a deep understanding of their business strategy and strategic goals, to advise on Human Resources matters including employee relations, performance management, workforce planning, and organizational development   Works closely with operations management and employees to support and drive a positive and inclusive culture. Facilitates strategies designed to foster employee engagement and retention Provides guidance and counsel on employee relations matters, including conducting investigations in compliance with university policies and applicable laws. Partners with leadership to address and resolve employee concerns and recommends appropriate corrective action when necessary Supports performance management efforts by advising on goal setting, coaching, and development strategies. Provides resources and training recommendations to strengthen manager capability and performance outcomes Serves as a liaison to Human Resources. Provides expert policy guidance and interpretation. Ensures compliance with federal and state regulations along with university policies, procedures, and practices Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of HR administration including talent acquisition, compensation, performance management, and employee relations principles and best practices Skill in analytical and critical thinking to develop solutions to business and people issues and use data analytics to support insights and develop actions Skill in written, verbal, and interpersonal communication to influence and articulate a variety of topics to different and diverse audiences Ability to work independently and with a team in a fast-paced environment Ability to handle sensitive situations with empathy, cultural awareness, and confidentiality Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in related field 5 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Specialized Contributor Level 3 - A senior-level role requiring broad understanding of the profession or field of work. Independently leads diverse and often complex assignments, projects, or programs. May act as a mentor and guide less experienced staff. FLSA Category Exempt Work Location Hybrid Compensation $85,000 to $115,000 Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
