    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Rochester-NY/Software-Engineer_JR102061": {
      "title": "Slate Engineer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights We are seeking a technical professional with hands-on experience administering, configuring, developing, and supporting solutions within Technolutions Slate, ideally with experience in Slate Student Success. This role is best suited for individuals who have served as a technical administrator, engineer, developer, or solution architect and who are comfortable taking ownership of platform design, configuration, testing, documentation, deployment, and ongoing support. The position serves as the lead technical resource for Student Affairs' Slate Student Success implementation and requires the ability to translate business needs into scalable, sustainable technical solutions. To receive full consideration, applicants must submit both a resume and cover letter. Flexible work arrangements are available, including remote, hybrid, or on-campus options. Successful candidates will have: Hands-on experience configuring, developing, and supporting solutions within Technolutions Slate, preferably Slate Student Success. Experience building and maintaining workflows, forms, communications, portals, automations, rules, queries, and other platform-based solutions. Experience serving as a technical administrator, engineer, developer, or solution architect for a Slate environment. Experience testing, troubleshooting, documenting, deploying, and supporting technical solutions throughout their lifecycle. Strong collaboration skills, with the ability to partner effectively with functional stakeholders, technical teams, and vendors. The ability to communicate technical concepts clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences. Experience in higher education, student affairs, student success, or similarly complex service-oriented environments preferred. Knowledge of accessibility-centered practices, inclusive technologies, Lean Six Sigma, or continuous improvement methodologies preferred. Role Scope and Responsibilities The Slate Engineer serves as the technical lead for Student Affairs' Slate Student Success implementation. This position is responsible for designing, configuring, testing, documenting, deploying, maintaining, and enhancing technical solutions within the Slate platform. Key responsibilities include: Building and maintaining Slate-based workflows, forms, portals, communications, automations, rules, queries, and related platform solutions. Translating functional needs into technical designs that balance immediate priorities with long-term sustainability. Testing and troubleshooting Slate solutions to ensure they are launch-ready, reliable, and aligned with divisional and university requirements. Creating and maintaining documentation, standards, and repeatable processes so solutions can be supported beyond initial implementation. Supporting implemented services across their lifecycle, including monitoring, issue resolution, enhancements, and refinements as needs evolve. Partnering with Student Affairs stakeholders, RIT Information Technology Services, and vendors on integrations, infrastructure needs, system improvements, and technical problem-solving. Representing Student Affairs in cross-functional technology conversations related to Slate Student Success and related systems. Communicating technical concepts in clear, accessible language for diverse audiences. Supporting technology solutions with attention to data integrity, information security, accessibility, and inclusive user experiences. Systems & Business Analysis for the Division of Student Affairs The Slate Engineer is part of the Systems and Business Analysis team within the Division of Student Affairs. The team supports technology systems, business processes, data integrity, information security, and sustainable operational solutions that help Student Affairs departments deliver services to students. Within this team, the Slate Engineer serves as the lead technical resource for Student Affairs' Slate Student Success implementation. The role focuses on designing, implementing, and sustaining Slate-based solutions that support coordinated communication, workflow management, student engagement, and divisional operations. This position provides an opportunity to help shape how Student Affairs uses Slate as a scalable platform to support students and staff across the division.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Creates, tests, documents, deploys, and supports software applications for multiple products and platforms Supports software solutions by studying information needs; conferring with users; studying systems flow, data usage, and work processes; investigating problem areas; and following the software development lifecycle Performs coding, debugging, unit testing, troubleshooting and modification of product software Participates in efforts to identify and implement best practices and data standards for the division. Ensures that services are supported, monitored, and maintained throughout the life cycle Creates and maintains documentation for supported services Troubleshoots performance issues and partners with other teams and vendors to implement improvements Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of systems development lifecycle and industry best practices Knowledge of enterprise resource planning systems Skill in software integration Skill in advising groups on systems, networks, software, applications, and security issues Ability to design, document, test, create, or modify computer programs Ability to apply systems analysis techniques and procedures ​ Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in related field 2 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Specialized Contributor Level 2 - A fully functional role requiring established knowledge of the profession or field of work. Responsible for completing substantive assignments and projects. Problems are varied and non-routine, and resolution requires exercising judgment, analysis, advisement, creativity, and understanding broader sets of issues. May provide assistance to entry level staff. FLSA Category Exempt Work Location Remote Compensation $72,500 - $95,000 Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Rochester-NY/Golisano-Outreach-Archives-Assistant_JR102638": {
      "title": "Golisano Outreach Archives Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights The Marie Golisano Graham Outreach Archives Assistant Fellowship position supports public-facing initiatives that engage the RIT community with the B. Thomas Golisano collection in RIT Archives. This position will be working for an eighteen-month project term under the guidance of the Innovation & Engagement Archivist. Key responsibilities include:   Develop physical and digital exhibits related to the B. Thomas Golisano collection.  Collaborate with RIT faculty to teach with and integrate Golisano collection materials into their classes.  Conduct oral history projects that enhance collection interpretations and profile individuals related to the life and legacy of B. Thomas Golisano.  Coordinate logistics for events and public programs related to the Golisano collection.  Communicate in collaborative partnership with the Golisano Foundation to support Fellowship goals.  Contribute to the creation of digital content that increases accessibility and engagement with the Golisano collection.  Provide general support and perform shared responsibilities within RIT Archives; including: assisting with reference requests; project-based work; attending department meetings; updating, planning, and/or establishing departmental policies and workflows.  The Marie Golisano Graham Outreach Archives Assistant Fellowship model was recently established to honor its namesake donor’s dual commitments to long-term engagement with the B. Thomas Golisano collection, and to supporting early-career individuals at a critical point in their professional development. Recent graduates of Library and Information Science, Museum Studies, Public History or related degree programs will have a unique opportunity to bridge the gap between pursuing advanced study or entering the workforce; and gain intensive hands-on experience in archival outreach, student-centered advocacy within university environments, curation, and living donor relations under professional mentorship.  About the B. Thomas Golisano collection  Blase Thomas “Tom” Golisano (b. 1941) is an entrepreneur, philanthropist, civic leader, mentor, and change-maker for Western New York and Southwest Florida communities. In 1971, he founded Paychex, Inc., a leading national provider of payroll services for small businesses, and served as its President and CEO until his retirement in 2004.  In 1985, Golisano established the Golisano Foundation, one of the largest private foundations in the United States supporting initiatives for individuals with intellectual and developmental disabilities (IDD). His philanthropic contributions, both personal and through the Golisano Foundation, now exceed $1 billion, including state-of-the-art healthcare facilities and educational institutions like RIT.  The B. Thomas Golisano collection was donated to RIT Archives by his sister Marie Golisano Graham in 2015, and spans Golisano’s personal and professional lives from 1965 to present. Since 2022, the collaborative partnership between RIT Archives and the Golisano Foundation has supported dynamic outreach initiatives with the B. Thomas Golisano collection, which continues to accrue as part of this living donor relationship.      Essential Duties & Responsibilities Monitors, organizes, and maintains library stacks to ensure accurate shelving, accessibility, and preservation of materials Assists with collection assessment projects, identifies duplicate items, and coordinates removal or relocation as needed Processes incoming donations and transfers by creating accession records, labeling materials, and ensuring proper documentation Updates and manages collection management systems, tracking the location, condition, and status of archival and library holdings Prepares materials for exhibitions, displays, and external loans under supervision. Assists in installation and deinstallation of exhibits, event setup, and public program logistics Participates in library committees, working groups, and outreach initiatives. Helps during tours, instructional sessions, or community engagement programs to promote awareness of archives and special collections Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of archival principles, practices, tools, and systems Knowledge of management, preservation, and archival of for born-digital and digitized materials Skill in appraising, processing, and describing archival collections Skill in transferring content from legacy media for archival purposes Ability to work as a part of a team Ability to develop and maintain effective and positive working relationships Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in related field 1 year of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Operations, Administrative, Service, or Technical Support Level 2 - An intermediate level role with working foundational knowledge and skills to perform routine and occasionally non-routine tasks. Tasks may require interpretation or deviation from standard procedures. May provide assistance to entry level staff. FLSA Category Non-Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $17.90-$25.00 per hour Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Rochester-NY/Senior-Financial-Analyst_JR102497": {
      "title": "Senior Financial Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights This position is centralized within the Division of Student Affairs and is part of the Financial Planning & Business Operations unit. The unit partners with Division and University stakeholders to support the planning, implementation, and evaluation of financial and human resources functions across the Division. This position is fully on campus and is not eligible for remote work. To receive full consideration, applicants must submit both a resume and cover letter with their application. Key responsibilities include: •    Division-level monitoring and reporting for Gift Commitments and associated Project Accounts •    Financial Specialist for Assessment, Technology & Communications & Student Development, Access & Support departments •    Grant financial administration and Division liaison to Sponsored Programs Accounting •    Collaborates closely with campus partners including Controller’s Office, Budget and Facilities •    Provides financial training and ongoing support for finance positions within the Division  The successful candidate will collaborate closely with University partners, including the Controller's Office, Budget Office, and Facilities Management. Experience managing multi-year budgets and working with diverse funding sources, such as gifts, grants, and capital project funds, is strongly preferred.   Student Affairs Financial Planning and Business Operations The Student Affairs Financial Planning and Business Operations team oversees the Division’s financial and workforce resources. Responsibilities include managing a $46 million operating budget, $17 million in annual revenue, and $8 million in gifts and discretionary funds across a variety of funding sources. The team supports the Senior Vice President in developing the Division’s financial strategy, allocating resources to advance priorities, and planning for all revenue and funding streams. It also provides Division level workforce planning and talent development for more than 300 staff positions while partnering with divisional leaders to achieve strategic goals. The Student Affairs Division’s strategic priorities of inclusion, community and belonging, well-being, and a unified organizational culture closely align with the university’s institutional priorities and strategic framework.    Essential Duties & Responsibilities Designs, prepares, and presents financial information to the leadership team to assist with ongoing management and decision making regarding the college’s finances and operations Maintains analysis and financial forecasting across the organization, including complex compensation-related reconciliations Prepares cost models based on data from general ledger, registrar, student financial services, and fixed assets Completes and evaluates complex reconciliations and analysis of financial accounts, including operating, capital, special, discretionary, start-up, internal grants, and overhead project accounts to ensure transactions are accurate and in compliance with applicable institution policies and other regulatory requirements Develops annual operating budget based on current salary recommendations, current and new academic and operational initiatives, and revenue forecasts Prepares various standard and ad hoc reporting and analysis for management decision-making for multiple stakeholders Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of accounting, finance, and budgeting practices and protocols to ensure accurate financial management and compliance Knowledge of enterprise-wide financial applications and Microsoft Office Skill in synthesizing and analyzing financial data and preparing detailed reports to support decision-making and budgeting activities Skill in written, verbal, and interpersonal communication and customer service Ability to manage multiple tasks and projects while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail Ability to work independently with minimal supervision and exercise professional judgment regarding financial decisions Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in related field 5 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Specialized Contributor Level 3 - A senior-level role requiring broad understanding of the profession or field of work. Independently leads diverse and often complex assignments, projects, or programs. May act as a mentor and guide less experienced staff. FLSA Category Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $65,900 - $75,000 Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
    },
    "https://rit.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Rochester-NY/Student-Financial-Aid-Advisor_JR102527-1": {
      "title": "Student Financial Aid Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Highlights Provides frontline assistance to students and families navigating the admissions and financial aid processes. Counsels students and families on financial aid programs and requirements, eligibility, and billing. Ensures compliance with relevant regulations and provides clerical support, including data entry, filing, and coordination for recruitment and financial aid events. Key responsibilities include: Under the direction of the Senior Assistant Director, the Student Financial Aid Advisor serves as the primary point of contact for prospective and current students, families, alumni, faculty, staff, and external agencies regarding all aspects of federal, state, institutional, and private financial aid programs. Advisors provide comprehensive financial counseling in-person, by telephone, email, and live chat, while ensuring exceptional customer service in a fast-paced, high-volume environment.   Essential Duties & Responsibilities Responds to inquiries from students, parents, and campus staff regarding admission status, financial aid programs, requirements, eligibility, application procedures, form completion, award status, and deadlines Educates students and families regarding student account statements and bill estimates Counsels and advises students and families regarding financial aid eligibility, application procedures, aid programs, costs, indebtedness, money management and financial planning. Facilitates appeal processes as needed Supports recruitment and financial aid events through event coordination tasks Performs data entry and record-keeping activities to track and maintain student records. Ensures data accuracy and compliance Provides general office administration support such as ordering supplies, greeting visitors, filing invoices and purchase orders, greeting visitors, and answering phone calls and emails Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of financial aid programs, including scholarships, emergency loans, and eligibility requirements Knowledge of administrative procedures and practices Skill in written, verbal, and interpersonal communication Ability to manage multiple tasks and projects while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail Ability to maintain a high level of confidentiality when handling sensitive information Minimum Education & Experience Associate's degree in related field 3 years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of experience and education may be considered Job Level Overview Operations, Administrative, Service, or Technical Support Level 2 - An intermediate level role with working foundational knowledge and skills to perform routine and occasionally non-routine tasks. Tasks may require interpretation or deviation from standard procedures. May provide assistance to entry level staff. FLSA Category Non-Exempt Work Location On Campus Compensation $17.90 - $28.60 Hourly Application Materials When you are ready to complete an application for this position please be prepared to submit the below requested information.  This will be required to ensure your application is processed in a timely manner. Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae or Resume Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. Additional Details In compliance with NYS's Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is listed above. Rochester Institute of Technology considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as, market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The hiring process for this position may require a criminal background check and/or motor vehicle records check. Any verbal or written offer made is contingent on satisfactory results, as determined by Human Resources. RIT provides equal opportunity to all qualified individuals and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, creed, age, marital status, sex, gender, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, veteran status or disability in its hiring, admissions, educational programs and activities. RIT provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities under the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the New York Human Rights Law, or similar applicable law. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please contact the Human Resources office at 585-475-2424 or email your request to  careers@rit.edu . Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis."
