      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEssential Duties & Responsibilities Serves food to diners following established quality control, portioning, and customer service standards Maintains the cleanliness and organization of serving lines, condiment stations, and dining areas Sets up and breaks down serving stations in accordance with dining service requirements Follows all sanitation and health safety standards strictly Provides excellent service in a friendly, sincere, and courteous manner Confirms supplies and equipment availability and oversees setup as necessary Other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities Knowledge of food service sanitation and safety procedures Skill in high-volume dining customer service Skill in verbal, written, and interpersonal communication Ability to deliver exceptional customer service Ability to collaborate with team members in a fast-paced environment Minimum Education & Experience High School diploma or GED No experience required Job Level Overview Operations, Administrative, Service, or Technical Support Level 1 - An entry-level role building knowledge and skills. Performs routine, well-defined, easy-to-understand tasks that can typically be learned in a short period of time. Work is performed under close supervision using clearly prescribed methods and detailed instructions.   Why Work for RIT Dining RIT Dining serves thousands of students, faculty, and staff each day, creating meaningful moments across campus. As a university‑owned operation, we’re committed to delivering personalized culinary experiences while providing valuable growth opportunities for both full‑time employees and student workers. You’ll work alongside a diverse team, including students from many backgrounds—to create a welcoming, inclusive environment. Your contributions enhance the student experience as customers and support employees in building the teamwork, confidence, and real‑world skills that 